[center][b]The Commonwealth family: made to work together[/b]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport[/url]: runs the scenes · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109225]Chemistry[/url]: NPCs find each other · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109433]Overture[/url]: you talk someone into it · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url]: working genitals, arousal and contact · [b]Anatomy Engine[/b] (this page): the physics behind them · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109439]Silhouette[/url]: everyone gets a body of their own · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/games/fallout4/collections/dmt85e]Ivy's Panties[/url]: all of it, installed for you[/center]

[center][size=4][b]New here? [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6679]The setup guide[/url]: from the body to the scenes, in one order, with what to take and what to skip.[/b][/size][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]In short[/color][/b][/size]

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Body parts that touch each other push each other, and nothing snaps or shakes. Breasts, butt, anything your physics file collides.[/*]
[*]With Anatomy: genitals that open around what touches them, and a penis that finds the right opening in any animation pack.[/*]
[*]With Anatomy: a mouth that fits what is at the lips, and our own sex sounds in scenes.[/*]
[*]With Rapport: her face and eyes in a scene, including looking up into her partner's eyes now and then.[/*]
[/list][b]What you need[/b]: F4SE and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url]. For the genitals, mouth and aim, you also need [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url].
[b]How it goes[/b]: install it with Vortex or MO2, and let this engine's cbp.dll win over any other one. Details: [b]Before you play[/b], below.

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]What it is[/color][/b][/size]

The Anatomy Engine (fo4-ocbpc) is OCBPC, the physics-with-collisions [font=Courier New]cbp.dll[/font], extended. It is a fork of [url=https://github.com/ericncream/OpenCBP_FO4]ericncream's OpenCBP_FO4[/url], the code behind OCBPC 0.3, and it replaces that one file.

It is the engine under [b]Anatomy[/b], and it is what lets [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport[/url] own the face in a scene. Without Anatomy, it is OCBPC with a collision bug fixed: every OCBPC config collides better with it.

How it works, in full: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6674]The physics engine[/url].

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]What you get[/color][/b][/size]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-ocbpc@5b6d9837d62b2c86fc7e26e83d6282d1e7e8f185/docs/img/sounds.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Sex sounds from the engine.[/b] Every animation pack's built-in sounds are muted in scenes. Our own set, matched in loudness, plays from how deep and how fast each stroke really is. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6675]Arousal and sex →[/url][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Men too (M-M):[/b] men are simulated for Anatomy's bones even under a women-only preset, and the penis aims into the men's anus.[/*]
[*][b]Contact without jitter:[/b] tight contact holds firm, so nothing shakes when it squeezes.[/*]
[*][b]A health check:[/b] after every load, Anatomy_Health.txt names the engine, the preset, the body and the characters it moves; after your first AAF scene it adds who was in it, whether her openings were found, and what to fix when they weren't. A message box appears only on a real problem.[/*]
[*][b]Anatomy's own preset follows the body you built[/b] (CBBE or 3BBB).[/*]
[*][b]An installer:[/b] a setup check, then one page per feature. Install with Vortex or MO2; installing by hand is not supported.[/*]
[/list][center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-ocbpc@4fd97d389a06af8af74607de29174308dd41a491/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]
[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]For every OCBPC user[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Each collision pushes once per frame.[/b] OCBPC could push a bone twice near a cell edge, and it snapped back the next frame. Breasts, butt, anything your config collides: pushed once.[/*]
[*][b]Hooks that check first.[/b] Every hook reads the game's code before patching it and stays off, logged, on any other build. If installing the eye or the mouth hook fails, that one feature turns off instead of crashing the game.[/*]
[*][b]A log two game processes can't break.[/b] Relaunching after a crash no longer wipes the running game's log.[/*]
[*]Built with today's compiler, statically linked, with the same imports and exports as the original.[/*]
[/list][center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-ocbpc@4fd97d389a06af8af74607de29174308dd41a491/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]With Anatomy[/color][/b][/size]

Anatomy's own config switches these on; without it, they stay off.

[list]
[*][b]One smooth tube, not a string of balls.[/b] OCBPC reads a penis as five balls with gaps between them, so flesh rode in and out along a thrust. Measured on the real mesh: thrust wobble at the anus 0.69 → 0.21, at the vagina 0.26 → 0.13 (the card above).[/*]
[*][b]Bones added while the game runs.[/b] The genital bones are added under each actor's pelvis as she loads. No skeleton file is shipped or overwritten.[/*]
[*][b]The penis finds its opening.[/b] In an AAF scene it turns toward the opening the animation meant. It bends along a measured path instead of poking through the body, follows the throat when the head tilts back, and follows a gripping hand.[/*]
[*][b]Lips that fit.[/b] Fallout 4 heads have no mouth bones, so the engine uses 15 measured mouth shapes every frame to rest the lips on whatever crosses them, and closes them between strokes.[/*]
[*][b]A shape per man:[/b] a thinner shaft and a bigger head, set on his bones while the game runs. BodyTalk4's files are untouched.[/*]
[/list][i]The genital bones stay attached on women outside your own cell, and settle back to rest after a ragdoll.[/i]

